    "abstract": "Indian Journal of Ecology (Indian J Ecol) is the official Journal of the Indian Ecological Society, published since 1974 (ISSN-0304-5250). A peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to ecological research.",
    "field": "Avian ecology",
    "problem": "The paper addresses how anthropogenic pressures and climate change cause a \"species drift,\" where avian communities shift from wetland-dependent birds to dry-habitat species, indicating significant ecosystem degradation even when the total number of species does not decline, thus challenging traditional biodiversity assessment methods.",
    "method": "This study investigates avian species drift by performing a comparative analysis of 45 species at Jigani Lake, using e-bird data and personal documentation from 2020 to 2024 to identify changes in migratory patterns resulting from habitat destruction and climate variation.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze bird species drift and migratory pattern changes at Jigani Lake, Bangalore, caused by habitat destruction and climate variation, using observational and eBird data from 2020 to 2024.",
